# Mines an asteroid with the mining laser and scoops what it splits into. It starts from mining-laser.cdr
# (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the reference's own save with fuel scoops and a mining laser for the pulse laser, as the
# equipment screen fits them, and its random state 13 draws on, which puts an asteroid ahead of the launch. I, held
# while the asteroid is in the sights, identifies it (ShowShipIdentity: CLASS: Debris TYPE: Astroid) and locks a missile
# on it; the mining laser, fired once it is within 1,200 units, splits it into splinters (SpawnFragments, with the
# slower scatter and the longer life a mined asteroid gives them), and three are scooped, each Metal Alloys
# (TryScoopObject). Asteroids are rare at Lave without the jump drive: a search of 3,000 draw counts found one in the
# first seconds of space only at 13. The flight was played by a scratch program that steered at the asteroid by its
# position each frame, slowed and fired within range, then steered each splinter under the nose at low speed; what it
# pressed is recorded here like any other replay.
file JAMESON.CDR mining-laser.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # D10, Disc access, on Load commander
key 1; wait 0.3                    # Load commander: the catalogue, JAMESON.CDR selected
key Return; wait 0.5               # loaded
